From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:40:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Back up on every app open, with rotation, and fix the silent
 auto-export

The periodic zip export could silently stop producing backups (WorkManager is unreliable on aggressive vendor ROMs, and every app start re-enqueued the work with CANCEL_AND_REENQUEUE), and it always overwrote one fixed file opened with mode "wt", so a failed export truncated the only backup the user had. A user lost weeks of data that way.

Backup on app open (no background scheduling, no keep-alive):
- New OnOpenBackupRunner writes a full zip backup (db, preferences, external files) every time the launcher activity is opened, off the main thread.
- Every run creates a new gadgetbridge_yyyyMMddHHmmss.zip; nothing existing is touched, so a failed run can never destroy a previous backup.
- The zip is exported to a cache temp file, validated, and only then copied into the target: into a SAF directory the user picked, or the app's backups/ folder by default.
- Retention keeps the last N days (3/7/14/30, default 7) of our own backups, always keeping the newest one, and never deletes files it did not write.
- Skips when nothing changed since the last backup, so app opens do not fill the storage with identical copies.

Auto-export fixes:
- PeriodicExporter no longer cancels and re-enqueues the work on every app start (ExistingPeriodicWorkPolicy.UPDATE, cancelUniqueWork only when disabled).
- ZipBackupExportJob exports into a temporary file, validates it, and only then writes the target, deleting the partial target if the copy fails.
- The zip auto-export location picker now picks a directory, so its runs are timestamped and rotated too.

Material 3 settings screen:
- New OnOpenBackupSettingsActivity with an MD3 preference screen (switch, folder picker, retention list, run now, clean now, status), reachable from Settings > Automations and indexed for settings search.
- SettingsActivity, automations_settings.xml, strings and arrays updated; no Material2/AppCompat theme introduced.
